  "caption": "Instrumental original handheld JRPG reflective cue in D major, 3/4, 82 quarter-note BPM. Preserve the complete supplied 20-bar independent melody, varied phrase rests, explicit scene-specific support and bass. piano lead with strings support. Clean restrained timbres, no extra notes or reharmonization, no distortion, vocals or fade.",
  "form_description": "20 bars in 3/4: eight-bar original piano farewell; four-bar warming string bridge; four-bar augmented title call and answer at the late arrival; four-bar piano coda. Only bars 13-16 quote the original main theme, at one-and-a-half times its original durations.",
  "reference_tracks": [
    3,
    103,
    106
  ],
  "composition_notes": "Independently authored literal tune, meter, form and groove for this region. Scalar passing notes retain their melodic shape while accompaniment thins to a consonant single tone or dyad; they are not forced into arpeggiated triads. A nearest-motion triadic anchor path guides harmonic direction. Independently selected bass avoids exposed parallel fifths/octaves, and scene-specific rests break its automatic doubling of the lead rhythm. Actual score and MIDI events are separately audited; this is not a claim of human listening approval.",
